{"name":"Feels Good Man","hex":"#7ca25a","fetched":"2026-10-18","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"feels","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of feel, sensory perceptions that mainly or solely involve the sense of touch"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Feelings; emotions; especially, tender sentiment."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/feels"},{"term":"good","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a person or an animal.","Competent or talented."]},{"part":"Interjection","definitions":["That is good; an elliptical exclamation of satisfaction or commendation."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/good"},{"term":"man","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-2 & ISO 639-3 language code for Mandingo."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An adult male human.","All human males collectively: mankind."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/man"}],"entries":[{"title":"Feels Good Man","blocks":[{"text":"Feels Good Man is a 2020 American documentary film about the Internet meme Pepe the Frog. Marking the directorial debut of Arthur Jones, the film stars artist Matt Furie, the creator of Pepe. The film follows Furie as he struggles to reclaim control of Pepe from members of the alt-right who have co-opted the image for their own purposes. The film premiered at the 2020 Sundance Film Festival and won a U.S. Documentary Special Jury Award for Emerging Filmmaker. It was also nominated in the U.S. Documentary Competition at Sundance."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/b0/Feels_Good_Man_poster.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Feels_Good_Man","wikidata":"Q84427809"},{"title":"Pepe the Frog","blocks":[{"text":"Pepe the Frog is a comic character and Internet meme created by cartoonist Matt Furie. Designed as a green anthropomorphic frog with a humanoid body usually wearing a blue t-shirt, Pepe originated in Furie's 2005 webcomic Boy's Club. The character became an Internet meme when his popularity steadily grew across websites such as Myspace, Gaia Online, and 4chan from 2008 onwards; by 2015, he had become one of the most popular memes on 4chan and Tumblr."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/63/Feels_good_man.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pepe_the_Frog","wikidata":"Q21994166"},{"title":"Feels Good","blocks":[{"text":"\"Feels Good\" is a number-one R&B single by Tony! Toni! Toné! featuring a rap verse by Mopreme Shakur. The hit song spent two weeks at number 1 on the U.S. R&B chart, and it peaked at number 9 on the U.S. Billboard Hot 100. \"Feels Good\" also peaked at number 3 on the dance charts."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/6c/Tony_Toni_Tone_Feels_Good.PNG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Feels_Good","wikidata":"Q5441408"},{"title":"Good","blocks":[{"text":"In most contexts, the concept of good denotes the conduct that should be preferred when posed with a choice between possible actions. Good is generally considered to be the opposite of evil. The meaning and etymology of the term and its associated translations among ancient and contemporary languages show substantial variation in its inflection and meaning, depending on circumstances of place and history, or of philosophical or religious context."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Good","wikidata":"Q15290"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/b/b0/Feels_Good_Man_poster.jpeg/250px-Feels_Good_Man_poster.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/b0/Feels_Good_Man_poster.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thu